<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0in"><B><U>Notes:</U></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0in">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 0.25in">(1)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify; padding-right: 1.8pt">The Company has agreed
                                            to pay the Underwriters a cash commission (the &ldquo;<B>Underwriters&rsquo; Fee</B>&rdquo;)
                                            equal to <FONT STYLE="font-family: Wingdings"><B>l</B></FONT>% of the aggregate purchase
                                            price paid by the Underwriters to the Company for the Offered Shares. See &ldquo;<I>Plan
                                            of Distribution</I>&rdquo;.</TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD>(2)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify; padding-right: 1.8pt">After deducting the Underwriters&rsquo; Fee, but before deducting
                     the expenses of the Offering, which are estimated at US$<FONT STYLE="font-family: Wingdings"><B>l</B></FONT> and
                     will be paid by the Company from the proceeds of the Offering. The net proceeds payable to the Company will be derived
                     from the sale of the Offered Shares.</TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD>(3)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify; padding-right: 1.8pt">The Company has granted the Underwriters an over-allotment
                     option (the &ldquo;<B>Over-Allotment Option</B>&rdquo;), exercisable in whole or in part, at any time and from time
                     to time, in the sole discretion of the Underwriters, for a period of 30 days from the date of closing of the Offering,
                     to purchase up to <FONT STYLE="font-family: Wingdings"><B>l</B></FONT> additional Common Shares (the &ldquo;<B>Additional
                     Shares</B>&rdquo;) at the same price as set forth above, to cover overallotments, if any, and for market stabilization
                     purposes. See &ldquo;<I>Plan of Distribution</I>&rdquo;. If the Over-Allotment Option is exercised in full, the
                     total public Offering Price, Underwriters&rsquo; Fee and net proceeds to the Company (after deducting the Underwriters&rsquo;
                     Fee but before deducting the expenses of the Offering) will be US$<FONT STYLE="font-family: Wingdings"><B>l</B></FONT>,
                     US$<FONT STYLE="font-family: Wingdings"><B>l</B></FONT> and US$<FONT STYLE="font-family: Wingdings"><B>l</B></FONT>,
                     respectively.</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0pt">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0pt">The following table
sets out the number of Additional Shares for which the Over-Allotment Option may be exercised:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0pt">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse">
  <TR>
    <TD STYLE="border-bottom: Black 1pt solid; text-align: left; vertical-align: bottom; width: 34%"><P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0pt"><B>Underwriters&rsquo; Position</B></P></TD>
    <TD STYLE="width: 2%">&nbsp;</TD>
    <TD STYLE="border-bottom: Black 1pt solid; vertical-align: bottom; width: 20%; font-size: 10pt; text-align: center"><P STYLE="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"><B>Maximum Number of</B></P>
